# Refresh after changes (mandatory)

- After ANY change to code, config, Dockerfiles/compose files, scripts or assets, and before finishing the turn, you MUST read and follow `.cursor/skills/refresh-after-changes/SKILL.md`: rebuild/restart/redeploy-local the affected app(s), verify, and report what was refreshed and how.
- A task is NOT done until the change is live and verified. A passing build alone is not enough when the app is meant to be running.
- If this repo has a more specific refresh rule (e.g. a restart/rebuild rule), follow that rule for the how; this rule only makes the refresh mandatory.
- Skip only when the change is docs/comments-only (`*.md`, comments, `.cursor/**`), and say "Refresh skipped: docs-only".
- A `stop` hook (`.cursor/hooks/refresh-check.ps1`) re-prompts you if non-doc changes were left unrefreshed.
